‑head/valve‑cover assembly. No turbochargers—large, distinct units with compressor/turbine housings and inlet/outlet pipes—are present.  \n- **Setting:** A clean, well‑lit industrial workshop typical of Bugatti’s engine‑assembly line.\n\n**Verdict on the original claim (“They are installing the turbochargers”)**  \nThe claim is **incorrect**. The visual evidence clearly shows the technicians assembling the **valvetrain and installing the cylinder‑head/valve cover**, not mounting any turbochargers. Turbocharger installation would involve large external units and piping, which never appear in these frames.', 'failed_images': []}

